The final phase of the software testing process where users test the software to make sure it works as intended and meets business needs.

How it is Used

The user acceptance test is often completed before deploying new software for the public and/or internal departments to use. County IT employees may test software in an user environment to ensure it works well.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:1:{s:25:"glossary:software_testing";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1744831774;s:8:"modified";i:1744833509;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744833509;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:29:"glossary:user_acceptance_test";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:31;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}}